# What never enters a build context.
#
# Two rules, and the second is the one that matters:
#
#   1. Nothing that the image rebuilds anyway. `node_modules/`, `dist/` and `.next/` are produced
#      inside the build stage from the lockfile and the sources; copying a host copy in would make
#      the image depend on whatever the last local `pnpm build` happened to leave behind, and on
#      Windows it would copy `win32-x64` native optional dependencies into a `linux/amd64` image.
#
#   2. Nothing that is not needed to *run* the product. Documentation, the HTML mockups, CI
#      configuration and the wave scripts are all inputs to people, not to a container. Excluding
#      them is not a size optimisation — it is that a file inside an image is a file an attacker
#      who reaches the container can read.
#
# `migrations/` is deliberately NOT excluded: `packages/core/dist/db/migrate.js` reads
# `migrations/meta/_journal.json` at start-up and refuses to run without it.

# 1 — rebuilt inside the image
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
**/dist/
.next/
.next-embedded/
**/.next/
**/.next-embedded/
# @indx-workspace/embedded's packaged build (its Nx output); no image reads it, and CI restores it
# into the checkout, which must not change the context the images are built from.
packages/*/publish/
build/
**/build/
coverage/
**/coverage/
.terraform/
**/.terraform/
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
**/next-env.d.ts

# 2 — not needed to run the product
.git/
.github/
.claude/
docs/
ui/
tests/
internal/
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
# Agent and contributor instructions, the formal model, the marketing sites, and the repository's
# own build, test and lint configuration (BH061-059). The Dockerfiles themselves are read by the
# builder whether or not they are in the context; excluded here, no image can copy them.
AGENTS.md
**/AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
**/CLAUDE.md
ENGINEERING_GUIDELINES.md
llms.txt
formal/
sites/
Dockerfile
*.Dockerfile
compose.yaml
playwright*.config.*
vitest*.config.ts
knip.json
jscpd.json
dependency-cruiser.config.mjs
.trivyignore.yaml

# `LICENSE` is NOT excluded. Apache-2.0 §4(a) obliges us to give a copy of the licence to every
# recipient of the work, and an image is a distribution of the work.

# Never, under any circumstances. Patterns are anchored at the context root, so a bare `*.tfvars`
# would miss `infra/terraform/*/terraform.tfvars`: every secret-bearing pattern carries `**/`.
# Terraform plan and state files hold every variable in plaintext.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
**/*.tfvars
**/*.tfplan
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
